  "title": "96: al-Alaq العلق",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِقْرَاْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَۚ‏(1)\nIQRAA BISME RABBEKAL LAZEE KHALAQ.\nRead thou! (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) In the name of thy Lord Who created (Everything in the Universe)\nخَلَقَ الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍۚ‏(2)\nKHALAQAL INSAANA MIN A’LAQ.\nHe created man from a clot!\nاِقْرَاْ وَرَبُّكَ الْاَكْرَمُۙ‏(3)\nIQRAA WA RABBOKAL AKRAMUL.\nRecite (Thou O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) And thy Lord is the Most Honourable!\nالَّذِىْ عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِۙ‏(4)\nLAZEE A’LLAMA BIL-QALAME.\n(He) Who taught (to write) with the Pen\nعَلَّمَ الْاِنْسَانَ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْؕ‏(5)\nA’LLAMAL INSAANA MAA LAM YA’LAM.\n(He) taught man what he knew not!\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لَيَطْغٰٓىۙ‏(6)\nKALLAA INNAL INSAANA LA-YATGHAA.\nNay! Verily man is wont to rebel!\nاَنْ رَّاٰهُ اسْتَغْنٰىؕ‏(7)\nAR RA-AAHUS TAGHNAA.\nAs he deemeth himself needless!\nاِنَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ الرُّجْعٰىؕ‏(8)\nINNA ELAA RABBEKAR RUJ-A’A.\nVerily unto thy Lord (alone) is the return!\nاَرَءَيْتَ الَّذِىْ يَنْهٰىؕ‏(9)\nA-RA-AYTAL LAZEE YANHAA.\nHast, thou seen the man who forbiddeth?\nعَبْدًا اِذَا صَلّٰىؕ‏(10)\nA’BDAN EZAA SALLAA.\nA servant when he prayeth?\nاَرَءَيْتَ اِنْ كَانَ عَلَى الْهُدٰٓىۙ‏(11)\nA-RA-AYTA IN KAANA A’LAL HODAA.\nHast, thou seen if he were rightly guided?\nاَوْ اَمَرَ بِالتَّقْوٰىۙ‏(12)\nAW AMARA BIT-TAQWAA.\nOr enjoined piety?\nاَرَءَيْتَ اِنْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰىؕ‏(13)\nA-RA-AYTA IN KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\nHast, thou seen if he belieth the Truth and turneth (his) back?\nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمْ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَرٰىؕ‏(14)\nALAM YA’LAM BE-ANNAL LAAHA YARAA.\nKnowest he not that God seeth?\nكَلَّا لَئِنْ لَّمْ يَنْتَهِ ۙ لَنَسْفَعًۢا بِالنَّاصِيَةِۙ‏(15)\nKALLAA LA-IL LAM YANTAHE, LA-NASFA-A’M BIN-NAASEYATE.\nNay! (let him beware!) if he desisteth not, We shall surely drag him by the forelock!\nنَاصِيَةٍ كَاذِبَةٍ خَاطِئَةٍ ۚ‏(16)\nNAASEYATIN KAAZEBATIN KHAATE-ATAH.\nA forelock, lying, sinful!\nفَلْيَدْعُ نَادِيَهٗ ۙ‏(17)\nFAL-YAD-O’ NAADEYAHU.\nThen let him summon his fellows in council\nسَنَدْعُ الزَّبَانِيَةَ ۙ‏(18)\nSA-NAD-U’Z ZABAANEYATAH.\nWe too will summon the Angels of the Hell (to punish)\nكَلَّا ؕ لَا تُطِعْهُ وَاسْجُدْ وَاقْتَرِبْ۩‏(19)\nKALLAA, LAA TO-TE’HO WAS-JUD WAQ TARIB.\nNay! Heed him not! Prostrate thou in obeisance (unto thy Lord) and draw thyself near (unto Him)!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Alaq (The Clot)\nThere are 19 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that whoever recites this Surah in the daytime or at night, and then passes away, he will be counted amongst the martyrs who died while fighting on the side of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.).\nIt is highly recommended to recite this Surah while travelling and it acts as a safety from accidents. If recited on a treasure, it remains safe."
